==List of Areas==
Please note: GAMATOTO's level does not affect the drop amount nor general drop rate of items—it remains at 32% regardless of the area. Instead, each area has its own unique loot table; GAMATOTO levels work by decreasing the area's XP drop rate, then redistributing it between Cat Food, Battle Items, Catseyes, and other valuable goodies. There is also a massive redistribution spike at level 100, greatly increasing your odds at obtaining rarer items when compared to any other level threshold. You have to unlock the previous area before being able to unlock ones after.

''For battle item drops, see [[Battle Items|this page]] for an explanation. For Catseye drops, see [[Catseye|this page]] for an explanation.''

