==Expedition Helpers==
After each expedition, GAMATOTO has a rare chance (higher chance at Raisin' the Bar) to meet a fellow friend during the expedition, who joins him after the expedition ends. These are called "Expedition helpers" and take the form of smaller versions of GAMATOTO (without a costume). Helpers have a specific value attached to them based on their rank. Each point of value adds 0.27% to the base 32% item drop rate, up to a maximum of 50.9% at 10 Legend helpers. The value of each helper rank is as follows:

{| class="article-table" border="1"
! scope="col" |Helper Rank
! scope="col" |Value
|-
| Intern
| 1
|-
| Lackey
| 2
|-
| Underling
| 4
|-
| Assistant
| 6
|-
| Legend
| 7
|}

If your current helper lineup's aggregate value matches or exceeds 60, Legend helpers will replace Assistants in the helper pool.

Helpers come with randomly generated names selected from different sets for each rarity. The player can have at most ten helpers, and if an eleventh helper is found, at least one helper must be retired before GAMATOTO can be sent on an expedition again. If you try to start an expedition while having 11 helpers, a message will pop up letting you know and offering to dismiss one of the lowest rank helpers you have. By tapping on the helpers in the field, you can find the details of the helper's name and effect description, how many helpers you have and the dismiss button.

Dismissing a helper will allow them to be recruited to the [[Ototo Corps]] as engineers for use on [[Cat Base]] upgrades, if available. This is a useful way to obtain extra engineers if a helper is no longer needed (usually due to GAMATOTO finding one when the team is full), but players must ensure they do not have the maximum amount of them in order to avoid missing out on a free Engineer, as otherwise the dismissed helper is effectively wasted. Engineers gained this way are no different from normal ones and will be consumed after starting a project.

When the player has a good enough [[Cat Shrine|Cat Fortune]] (Li'l Luck or greater), there is a chance to summon Inari, who directly doubles all item rewards (no effect on [[Cat Food]]) at the end of an expedition, rather than increase the probabilities. Inari behaves like a regular helper for the rest, but doesn't count toward the helper limit, and will stay for only one expedition.

During certain collaboration events, a character from the collab will assist GAMATOTO in the same way as Inari. They will stay for every expedition during the collab only.

