==Trivia==
*GAMATOTO is revealed as Ototo's younger brother in [[Nyanko Daisensou ~Nippon Shinryaku Hiroku~]], even though Ototo's name (sounds like 弟 ''otōto'', or literally ''younger brother'') would suggest the opposite.
*GAMATOTO was mentioned in [[Masked Cat (Special Cat)|Masked Cat]]'s description before he was added to the game, then later in [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Stone Cat]]'s description and [[Burgle Boss Cat (Retired) (Special Cat)|Burgle Boss Cat (Prime)'s]] description.
**The costume unlocked at level 50 includes the same mask that Masked Cat wears. Furthermore, Stone Cat's description states that it was found by GAMATOTO. His level 116 outfit looks to have the bag of [[Burgle Boss Cat (Retired) (Special Cat)|Burgle Boss Cat]] from [[The Burgle Cats]], and Burgle Boss Cat (Prime)'s description says his protege, Gamatoto quit, forcing him to retire.
*The background changes depending on the actual time of day in your area. There are day, evening, and night backgrounds for each phase.
*If you decline to collect an Item Pack, a [[Doge]] will come to snatch the Item Pack and run away.
**If you decline the offer of a Great Fortune, the Doge will still come, stop for a split second, then run away, leaving the bag untouched.
*On occasion, a [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] can be seen in the tent.
*Raisin' the Bar may have been inspired by [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Patty%27s_Party_Planning_Place Patty's Party Planning Place], a bar where players can recruit new party members in the ''Dragon Quest'' series. The barkeep cat in Raisin' the Bar also has a similar hairstyle and hair color to [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Patty Patty] herself.
*The scenario "in the Chamber of Secrets." refers to the [[wikia:harrypotter:Chamber of Secrets|Chamber of Secrets]] from the ''Harry Potter'' series.
*The scenario "with a lewd kappa." refers to the ''[[wikipedia:Kappa (folklore)|kappa]]'', an amphibious, reptilian, humanoid ''yōkai'' with a penchant for cucumbers; this ''yōkai'' would later make an in-game appearance as [[Kappy Jr.]]
*Some of the possible [[Cat Shrine|Cat Fortunes]] are "Gamatoto will strike oil!" and "Gamatoto will dig it up!"
*His level 19 outfit looks somewhat like [[Hermit Cat (Special Cat)|Grandmaster Cat]].
*His level 67 outfit is based on an ''[[wikipedia:Oni|oni]]'', a type of ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'' often depicted with one or more horns and a ''[[wikipedia:Kanabō|kanabō]]''.
*His level 120 outfit looks somewhat like King Cat from [[Battle Cats Quest]].
*[[wikipedia:Inari Ōkami|Inari Ōkami]], or just Inari, is the Japanese ''[[wikipedia:Kami|kami]]'' of foxes, fertility, rice, agriculture, industry, and worldly success, to whom many have made offerings at her own [[wikipedia:Inari shrine|shrines]].
*The level MEGABANK is likely based on [[wikipedia:London|London]], due to featuring the [[wikipedia:122 Leadenhall Street|Leadenhall building]].
*The rarity of the helpers corresponds with the rarity of the cat units, specifically the color of the catseyes for each rarity. They as follows:
**Intern - Normal
**Lackey - Rare
**Underling - Super Rare
**Assistant - Uber Rare
**Legend - Legend Rare

